course: dictionary
lesson: 6509
title: Negative words and numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word negative has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one to use. In «The y position is 0 in the middle of the stage, bigger going up and negative below the middle», negative means less than zero, below the middle line. Numbers below zero have a minus sign, like -3.
explain: Negative can also mean "no". A negative answer to a question is a "no". It can mean bad or gloomy too. «An attack ad criticises the other candidate instead of praising your own» is called negative campaigning, because it focuses on what is bad.
explain: Negative can be good news as well. A negative test result means the thing being tested for was not found. Always check the context, then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Negative means less than zero when it is used with numbers, like -3 on a number line.
fact: Negative can mean saying "no", like a negative answer.
fact: Negative can mean bad, unhelpful or gloomy, as in a negative attitude.
fact: A negative test result means the thing tested for was not found.
fact: A negative sentence uses "not" or "no", and a double negative uses two negative words, which standard English avoids.
exercise: «From y = 0, up 20, up 20, down 50» gives what y? | *-10 | -50 | 10 | 40
exercise: What does negative mean in «a negative attitude»? | Less than zero | Saying yes | An old film photo | *Bad, unhelpful or gloomy
exercise: Mia's test says negative. What does this mean? | Mia's number is below zero | The test was lost in the post | The answer was yes | *The thing tested for was not found
test: A negative answer to a question means what? | Yes | Maybe | A number below zero | *No
test: Why is «An attack ad criticises the other candidate instead of praising your own» called negative campaigning? | *It focuses on criticising others and what is bad | It praises everyone equally | It uses a minus sign | It is a film photo
exam: Which use of negative means less than zero? | *The temperature fell to -5, a negative number | Her answer was a negative, meaning no | The lesson was negative and gloomy | A negative test result came back
